 "text": "Hey! How's everything going? That's very common fear. The first step is to drive it yourself for a while. Look for things you can do in a straight line, in your own time. A ten minute ride to work is better than a thirty minute commute that's stop start. And try riding in different weather, because city traffic is usually worse in the rain. Lots of people do. The best way to calm is practice. And once you' comfortable on your own, consider small group rides with other beginners.",
